---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<PageLayout
  meta={{
    title: 'About',
    description: 'About James, his learning focus, and this learning blog.'
  }}
  highlightColor='#659EB9'
>
  <main class='mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-12 py-16 sm:py-24'>
    <header class='flex flex-col gap-5'>
      <p class='text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground'>About</p>

      <h1 class='text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl'>About this blog</h1>

      <p class='text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground'>
        I’m James. I’m systematically learning programming, large language models, reasoning models,
        and the foundations of reinforcement learning. This website records how I build
        understanding through reading, hands-on implementation, and practical projects.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class='flex flex-col gap-4'>
      <h2 class='text-2xl font-semibold'>Why I write</h2>

      <p class='leading-7 text-muted-foreground'>
        I want to document what actually happens while learning: what I understand, where I get
        stuck, how I solve problems, and how my thinking changes through practice.
      </p>

      <p class='leading-7 text-muted-foreground'>
        Writing also forces me to turn vague understanding into clear explanations. If I cannot
        explain something clearly, I probably do not understand it well enough yet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='flex flex-col gap-4'>
      <h2 class='text-2xl font-semibold'>How I learn</h2>

      <ol class='flex list-decimal flex-col gap-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-muted-foreground'>
        <li>Choose a concrete project instead of reading theory alone.</li>
        <li>Divide the project into small, verifiable steps.</li>
        <li>Record problems, attempts, mistakes, and solutions.</li>
        <li>Turn the completed work into Chinese and English articles or notes.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class='flex flex-col gap-4'>
      <h2 class='text-2xl font-semibold'>Learning focus</h2>

      <div class='grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2'>
        <article class='rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-5'>
          <h3 class='font-semibold'>LLM and reasoning</h3>
          <p class='mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground'>
            Implementing model components from scratch to understand the foundations of language and
            reasoning models.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class='rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-5'>
          <h3 class='font-semibold'>RL</h3>
          <p class='mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground'>
            Studying the core ideas of reinforcement learning and their relationship to model
            training and decision-making.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class='rounded-2xl border border-border bg-muted/40 p-6'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>Find me</h2>
      <p class='mt-3 text-muted-foreground'>
        The source code and learning records for this blog are stored on GitHub.
      </p>
      <a
        class='mt-4 inline-block font-medium text-foreground underline underline-offset-4'
        href='https://github.com/jzc1296889459-maker'
        target='_blank'
        rel='noopener noreferrer'
      >
        github.com/jzc1296889459-maker
      </a>
    </section>
  </main>
</PageLayout>
